<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37962" body-key="">
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ</span></b> 
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ᾽ οὔατ᾽ ἀλεῖψαι ἑταίρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					12.47
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ οὔατα πᾶσιν ἄλειψα</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				177
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κηρὸν . . ὅν σφιν ἐπ᾽ ὠσὶν
				ἄλειψ᾽</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				200
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπόταν . . λεαίνῃ ἐπαλείφουσα τὰ
					τραχυνθέντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					66c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. χρόαν ἐτέραν ἐφ᾽ ἑτέραν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Sens.</u>
					440a9
				</span></i>
			: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς τοίχους τοὺς δύο
			ἐ.</span> 'run with the hare and hunt with the hounds', <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				6.3.15
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἐπαλειφθέν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ly.</u>
					217c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαλήλιπται ὁ κύτταρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					555a6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσὸς ἐπαληλιμμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					17.10.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., from anointing athletes,
				<i>prepare for contest, stir up, irritate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰ ἐπί τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					2.51.2
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τινάς τινι</span>
			<i>set</i> them <i>upon</i> him, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				2.38
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέθυσμα ἐ. θυμούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.680
				</span></i>
			; so perh. in physical sense, <i>irritate,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				1.99
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epid.</u>
				5.20
			</span></i>.</div>
	</div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
